#~ msgid ""
#~ "`int`，默认 0。`0` = Interstitial（体相插隙），在晶胞内随机采样位点放入额外原子；`1` ="
#~ " Adsorption（表面吸附），沿表面法向在表面上方放置原子。"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "`int`, default: `0`. `0` selects Interstitial "
#~ "mode, which samples positions inside the cell;"
#~ " `1` selects Adsorption mode, which places "
#~ "atoms above the surface along its normal."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Interstitial 模式下 `axis` 和 `offset` 不生效。Adsorption"
#~ " 模式需要 slab 输入，`axis` 决定了吸附原子沿哪条晶轴放。"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "`axis` and `offset` are ignored in "
#~ "Interstitial mode. Adsorption mode requires a "
#~ "slab input, and `axis` selects the cell "
#~ "direction along which adsorbates are placed "
#~ "above the surface."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "`str`，默认空。逗号分隔的元素列表，指定要插入什么原子。支持权重写法：`Li:0.7,Na:0.3` 表示每次随机放置时有 70%"
#~ " 概率插 Li，30% 概率插 Na。权重不写则等概率。"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "`str`, default: empty. Comma-separated elements "
#~ "to insert. Weighted entries are supported: "
#~ "`Li:0.7,Na:0.3` chooses Li with 70% probability "
#~ "and Na with 30% probability for each "
#~ "placement. Without weights, the elements are "
#~ "sampled uniformly."

#~ msgid "`int`，默认 1。每个生成结构里插几个额外原子。1~3 是常见范围——单原子插隙最容易放进去，数量越大碰撞失败概率越高。"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "`int`, default: `1`. Number of additional "
#~ "atoms in each generated structure. A typical"
#~ " range is 1–3. A single interstitial is "
#~ "easiest to place; larger counts increase the"
#~ " chance that placement fails because of "
#~ "collisions."

#~ msgid "`int`，默认 10。每输入帧生成多少个插入版本。"
#~ msgstr "`int`, default: `10`. Number of inserted variants generated for each input frame."

#~ msgid "10~50 做轻量验证，50~200 常规覆盖，200 以上建议接 `FPS Filter`。"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Use 10–50 for a lightweight check and "
#~ "50–200 for routine coverage. For more than "
#~ "200, follow this card with `FPS Filter`."

#~ msgid "几何约束"
#~ msgstr "Geometric constraints"

#~ msgid "`float`，默认 1.4。候选插入点与已有原子的最小允许距离，单位 Å。"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "`float`, default: `1.4`. Minimum allowed distance,"
#~ " in Å, between a candidate insertion point"
#~ " and every existing atom."

#~ msgid "对致密晶体，1.6~2.5 Å 比较保守安全；1.2~1.6 Å 是一个平衡点；压到 0.8~1.2 Å 碰撞风险明显升高，只有在你确信结构能容纳时才用。"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "For dense crystals, 1.6–2.5 Å is conservative;"
#~ " 1.2–1.6 Å balances acceptance and separation."
#~ " At 0.8–1.2 Å the collision risk rises "
#~ "substantially, so use such values only when"
#~ " the chemistry and available volume justify "
#~ "them."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "`int`，默认 200。每个待插入原子的最大随机尝试次数。增大它可以提高放置成功率，但耗时线性增长——如果你发现 200 "
#~ "次几乎每次都触顶失败，说明问题不是尝试次数不够，而是 `min_distance` 设大了或者胞太密。"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "`int`, default: `200`. Maximum random placement "
#~ "attempts for each atom to insert. Increasing"
#~ " it may improve acceptance but increases "
#~ "cost linearly. If nearly every insertion "
#~ "exhausts all 200 attempts, the real problem"
#~ " is usually an overly large `min_distance` "
#~ "or an excessively dense cell."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "`int`，默认 2。Adsorption 模式下它是表面法向。如果你的 slab 真空沿 z，默认"
#~ " 2（z 轴）就不用改；表面取向不同时一定要调，否则吸附高度方向会错。"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "`int`, default: `2`. Surface-normal axis in"
#~ " Adsorption mode. Keep the default `2` when"
#~ " the slab vacuum lies along *z*. Change "
#~ "it for a differently oriented surface; "
#~ "otherwise the adsorption height will be "
#~ "applied along the wrong direction."

#~ msgid "生效条件：涉及方向、分层、表面或向量初始化的模式都会使用。"
